# `pub` symbols in `internal/` packages that no other package calls, and the
# reason each stays `pub`. Read by check_internal_surface.sh: an unlisted one
# fails the build, and a listed one that gains a caller (or goes away) fails
# too, so the list cannot outlive its reasons.
#
# The bar is narrow. "A test uses it" is not a reason — an internal package's
# tests belong inside it, as `_wbtest.mbt`, where a package-private symbol is
# in reach. What earns a line here is a symbol that cannot be private either,
# because no production code calls it at all and `unused_value` rejects a
# private function in that state: an assertion that exists to be made and
# nothing else.
#
# Format: pkg/Symbol — reason
internal/column/BuiltinColumn::placeholders_normalized — the placeholder invariant every constructor, cast and transform is supposed to maintain; it exists to be asserted, so it has no production caller and cannot be private
